WEBVTT

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:15.120
Whoo!

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:22.360
In the heart of Africa, a young family is heading for an epic adventure.

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:30.920
They are moving with their three children to a remote Kenyan wilderness.

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:37.760
Mum, Saba, is here to run a safari camp...

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:38.680
Welcome.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:42.960
..While dad, Frank, is helping to protect elephants.

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:45.160
Collar's almost on, now the scary bit.

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:50.680
But raising a family and running a business in the bush is going to be a massive challenge.

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:51.600
Shoo!

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:54.440
There are monkeys in the kitchen...

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:54.920
Oh, you monkeys!

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:56.400
I'm going to kill you!

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:57.280
..Floods threatening the camp...

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:58.240
It's looking like it's going to be a megastorm.

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:00.000
..Medical emergencies...

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:02.000
It's bad, and it needs urgent action.

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:02.200
..And wildlife in need of help.

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:05.200
There is an elephant down.

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:08.680
It's going to be a huge gamble.

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:13.160
Will the business survive Saba's first season in charge?

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:13.360
Oh, my God.

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:23.960
This time, camp reopens after the rainy season.

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:24.640
I just feel like everything's kicking off, and it's quite exciting.

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:27.640
Guests are on their way...

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:29.360
You can't bring the guests here until we're done.

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:32.840
..But camp's falling apart.

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:33.320
Oh!

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:34.880
The main idea here is to keep the stress down.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:36.800
Frank is also under pressure.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:39.600
He's got an elephant with a problem...

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:43.360
We've not lost one yet, but we don't want to start now.

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:45.680
..And the situation becomes critical.

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:47.760
Now my heart really is in my mouth.

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:11.919
Elephant Watch camp has been closed for a month because of the rainy season.

00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:22.240
But in just one week, they'll reopen for guests and camp has to be rebuilt from scratch.

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:28.040
The family's new life depends on the business running successfully.

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:36.440
Guests come here for a luxury experience, but the wet weather in northern Kenya has taken its toll.

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:41.320
I've been taking all the tents down to get them fixed and sew up all the...

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:49.760
Get all the zips redone and replace all the netting, which has been...needed doing for ages.

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:57.120
It takes a day for a team of five to get a single tent up and ready.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:59.800
OK, fine, fine, fine.

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:02.280
You're right, I'm wrong.

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:02.920
Hello?

00:03:01.960 --> 00:03:08.160
They're counting on having seven days to get everything done.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:17.840
And I just get a call saying not only do I have one guest arriving into this room in half an hour, but supposedly I have another four pitching up at five o'clock this evening.

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:24.840
If the business is going to succeed, Saba can't afford to turn guests away.

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:31.600
But saying yes could backfire if they can't get the camp ready in time.

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:33.960
So, I'm in a bit of a panic.

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:37.200
And it's not just the tents that are worrying her.

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:39.280
Sim.

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:43.440
Now, listen, we've got a supplies problem.

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:46.840
I just don't think we've got enough cos they want to come for two nights.

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:47.200
Hi, Eleanor.

00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:47.880
Hi.

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:51.680
OK, look, if these four people are arriving, then we've got a serious problem.

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:55.520
We don't have anything in camp at the moment.

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:59.040
Saba's facing every host's worst nightmare.

00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:06.840
Vital supplies are missing, and right now she has nowhere for her guests to sleep.

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:10.640
You call them, I'm going to number five, OK?

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:14.480
The first visitor arrives in just half an hour.

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:18.079
I need all hands on deck pretty fast if we're going to get this done.

00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:19.720
What am I going to do?!

00:04:21.839 --> 00:04:28.280
Saba's husband, Frank, is also feeling the pressure.

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:34.840
He works for a conservation charity, Save The Elephants.

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:41.920
Today, he's tranquillising an elephant to fit a tracking collar.

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:46.400
It's a risky procedure and Frank is in charge of logistics.

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:53.600
The collaring we're going to be doing today is of a bull called Edison, who we've been wanting to get for a long time cos he's, er...

00:04:52.640 --> 00:05:04.840
He's an old friend of ours, a family friend, you could say, and he was just being kicked out of his family when this project started 17 years ago.

00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:13.960
So, he's a very interesting bull for us to get to know in terms of his movements.

00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:21.680
Male elephants leave the family unit as they reach sexual maturity, around the age of 12.

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:33.040
They cover huge distances in search of food and females.

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:40.960
Radio collaring them is invaluable in understanding their movements, and keeping them safe.

00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:41.520
We're at a time now where the price of ivory is at an all-time high.

00:05:40.680 --> 00:05:48.600
That means that the incentive to poach is that much increased and we're seeing it across the continent.

00:05:47.800 --> 00:06:02.320
Between 2010 and 2012, in those three years, 2010, 2011, 2012, Africa lost over 100,000 elephants, just in those three years.

00:06:01.760 --> 00:06:23.360
We don't really know how many elephants there are in Africa and that's part of the problem, but estimates are between 400,000 and 600,000, so to lose 100,000 in three years is just an astonishing rate of decline, and it just makes this whole situation so urgent.

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:37.920
Samburu National Reserve was once a safe haven for elephants.

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:45.120
But now a single pair of tusks could fetch over $100,000.

00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:53.920
With ivory prices so high, armed poachers are prepared to enter protected areas.

00:06:54.120 --> 00:07:02.640
Only last week, Koitelel, a well-loved bull elephant, was lost to poachers.

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:10.520
Frank's determined that no more elephants will die within the reserve this year.

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:21.280
He's arrived at the elephant research centre to brief the collaring team on the logistics for today.

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:21.680
Ah, morning!

00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:27.560
Tranquillising an elephant is risky and Frank needs all the help he can get.

00:07:26.760 --> 00:07:31.320
Morning, guys.

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:36.880
Chief scientist George Wittemyer has collared many elephants before.

00:07:36.040 --> 00:07:40.200
It's a huge responsibility.

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:44.640
Mistakes in this business can be fatal.

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:51.920
Just a few miles upriver, Saba's first guest has arrived.

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:55.880
Hello?

00:07:55.080 --> 00:07:59.600
I'm in number one, and you can't bring the guest here until we're done.

00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:02.600
Can you look after her?

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:09.320
OK, just give her drinks, make sure she's happy, tell her I'm just out and I'm coming in, in a second.

00:08:08.440 --> 00:08:10.400
She's arrived.

00:08:09.640 --> 00:08:10.800
Ooh!

00:08:11.680 --> 00:08:20.680
Camp manager Simeon is Saba's right-hand man and he's on his way to welcome the new guest.

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:28.560
We are looking forward to meet her and it's exciting because we've been working really hard to get the camp ready.

00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:33.960
In fact, they're still working hard.

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:41.600
Racing to finish the flooring... and cleaning the bathroom.

00:08:42.039 --> 00:08:44.120
Hello, Lisa.

00:08:43.280 --> 00:08:45.680
I'm so sorry I'm late.

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:46.800
Oh, no worries.

00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:47.520
Good to meet you.

00:08:46.640 --> 00:08:50.080
Welcome to Elephant Watch.

00:08:49.240 --> 00:08:50.720
Great to meet you, too.

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:57.200
Saba keeps Lisa talking just long enough for the team to finish the room.

00:08:56.240 --> 00:08:57.560
So, come in.

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:04.720
So, this is your tent.

00:09:03.760 --> 00:09:05.400
I'll show you round the front bit first.

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:07.160
This is your bathroom.

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:12.440
You come and you have your bush shower.

00:09:11.640 --> 00:09:13.040
All the water's heated by the sun.

00:09:12.120 --> 00:09:14.240
And here's your loo.

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:16.800
It's just a normal flush loo.

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:17.120
OK.

00:09:16.640 --> 00:09:24.120
And if you need anything, you've got a gown there to dress up in, you can come to dinner in that if you like, or breakfast, or whatever you feel like.

00:09:23.320 --> 00:09:26.160
Wow, OK.

00:09:25.360 --> 00:09:26.560
And if you need anything, just...

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:27.800
I'm always around so just let me know.

00:09:26.920 --> 00:09:28.240
OK.

00:09:27.440 --> 00:09:29.080
See you later.

00:09:28.360 --> 00:09:30.640
Bye-bye.

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:32.560
Got that done in the nick of time.

00:09:31.760 --> 00:09:35.360
She seems very happy, which is good.

00:09:36.560 --> 00:09:38.160
That's one guest settled.

00:09:37.240 --> 00:09:51.160
But there are still two more luxury rooms to create from scratch, with just five hours before the next group arrives.

00:09:51.040 --> 00:09:54.600
I think it's a help actually.

00:09:53.840 --> 00:10:05.720
Out in the reserve, Frank and the team are on their way to Edison, the bull they want to fit with a tracking collar.

00:10:04.920 --> 00:10:12.040
Like humans, every elephant responds differently to anaesthetic, so the team must be on their toes.

00:10:11.520 --> 00:10:13.560
It's going to be tense.

00:10:12.680 --> 00:10:20.880
Collaring a bull is a different story from collaring a female.

00:10:20.160 --> 00:10:27.280
We don't have the family to worry about, but they're a lot bigger, a lot stronger, and, erm...

00:10:26.760 --> 00:10:33.320
Yeah, they can be a bit more alarming, and sometimes they can have a bit more difficulty getting up afterwards.

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:38.720
So, yeah, we've not lost one yet, but we don't want to start now.

00:10:37.960 --> 00:10:45.080
But it's a risk worth taking.

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:49.080
Bull elephants range far beyond the safety of the reserve.

00:10:48.520 --> 00:10:55.120
Finding out where they go and why is crucial to help protect them.

00:10:54.160 --> 00:11:06.560
Their larger tusks also make them a valuable target for poachers... so keeping tabs on Edison is important.

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:08.200
It's Frank's job to make sure everyone is safe.

00:11:09.160 --> 00:11:15.280
Everybody's got to stay in their cars until explicitly told otherwise, OK?

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:19.560
And everyone's got to be as quiet as possible.

00:11:18.960 --> 00:11:29.360
The main idea here is to keep the stress down, because the quieter we can be and the more we can let the elephant be relaxed when the dart goes in, the better.

00:11:28.720 --> 00:11:34.720
OK, he's actually coming out of the bush now, so let's everyone just slowly get into the cars.

00:11:34.240 --> 00:11:35.320
We dart from here if we get a chance?

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:39.440
We dart from here if we get a chance.

00:11:39.240 --> 00:11:46.160
The team gets into position to administer the tranquilliser dart.

00:11:48.360 --> 00:11:53.400
OK, we will tell you, we're going to go up and...

00:11:57.800 --> 00:12:04.240
They will have to wait eight minutes for the sedative to take effect.

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:11.040
Until it does, Edison's reaction could be unpredictable.

00:12:10.160 --> 00:12:14.600
But there's an unexpected complication.

00:12:17.280 --> 00:12:22.320
Hey, Geronimo, there's some kids up above in the luga near the road.

00:12:21.440 --> 00:12:24.800
ON OK, shall I chase them away?

00:12:23.840 --> 00:12:27.120
Yeah, get those, there's some little kids.

00:12:26.560 --> 00:12:30.560
There's, like, three of them, just get them out of there.

00:12:29.640 --> 00:12:35.520
Some Samburu children and their goats have walked straight into Edison's path.

00:12:34.640 --> 00:12:37.960
A dangerous place to be.

00:12:37.160 --> 00:12:46.400
Certainly not something you expect inside a national park, to have kids running around with their goats.

00:12:45.560 --> 00:12:49.120
Yeah, it's just one of those extra variables that you don't think of.

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:53.640
This could upset the confused elephant.

00:12:52.880 --> 00:13:00.680
He looks pretty calm, but there's a risk that if he saw kids on foot he might go for them.

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:05.760
As soon as they saw the ranger, they just fled cos they thought they were in trouble.

00:13:04.840 --> 00:13:10.680
It looks like the goats are going another way, so that's hopefully that variable out the way.

00:13:12.480 --> 00:13:13.680
Edison's getting quite woozy.

00:13:13.200 --> 00:13:17.760
Six minutes.

00:13:17.640 --> 00:13:24.120
The sedative is taking effect.

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:27.600
There he goes.

00:13:26.800 --> 00:13:29.480
Just need to hope that he goes down on his side.

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:37.560
He's gone, he's gone.

00:13:38.840 --> 00:13:50.200
Too much tranquilliser in his system is dangerous, so they've given him as little as possible.

00:13:49.960 --> 00:13:57.720
They only have 20 minutes to fit the collar.

00:13:58.680 --> 00:14:07.240
Back at camp, Saba and the team only have a few hours to get the two tents up to scratch.

00:14:06.280 --> 00:14:07.800
We'll just see how this goes.

00:14:07.680 --> 00:14:11.400
Roger, OK, that's all right for now.

00:14:10.760 --> 00:14:18.640
SHE SPEAKS AFRICAN LANGUAGE Last minute or not, the guest accommodation must be absolutely perfect.

00:14:18.360 --> 00:14:25.560
Simeon, it's got to go literally, like, two inches that side, straight that way.

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:33.560
At the luxury end of the safari market, the devil is in the detail.

00:14:32.680 --> 00:14:37.640
They think I'm ridiculous because I'm so finickety about where everything is placed...

00:14:36.760 --> 00:14:41.240
..and they just think I'm insane.

00:14:40.280 --> 00:14:41.680
There we go.

00:14:40.800 --> 00:14:42.560
That's fine.

00:14:46.240 --> 00:14:58.000
With Saba so busy, it's lucky she has reinforcements to hand.

00:15:00.120 --> 00:15:03.840
Her three daughters are entertaining Lisa, the new guest... as only children can.

00:15:06.160 --> 00:15:11.160
I think you're speaking Swahili to me!

00:15:10.280 --> 00:15:14.080
I know you have no idea that I have no idea what you're saying.

00:15:16.880 --> 00:15:20.560
Meanwhile, there's a problem in one of the tents.

00:15:19.720 --> 00:15:22.680
Oh, my God, has this broken?

00:15:21.800 --> 00:15:23.400
Yeah.

00:15:22.560 --> 00:15:25.520
The sink in the bathroom is falling apart.

00:15:26.720 --> 00:15:33.880
Can we take it out and make it look nice or is it going to look like a disaster?

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:35.600
It's a disaster?

00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:36.680
Yeah.

00:15:35.800 --> 00:15:38.960
Oh!

00:15:38.040 --> 00:15:54.160
When we built this camp, the whole idea was to build it sort of under and around the trees so that you just got this feeling that you were sort of a little animal living under this amazing canopy.

00:15:53.440 --> 00:15:58.120
The downside is that everything moves and grows and changes.

00:15:57.160 --> 00:16:10.320
The branch is getting bigger and bigger, and heavier and heavier, the whole table is fixed onto it, so it's just broken this entire basin and I've got guests coming in about four hours.

00:16:09.480 --> 00:16:11.800
How this could happen today of all days...

00:16:11.120 --> 00:16:20.960
Thankfully, this bathroom has two sinks, so Saba just needs to clean up the mess and fill the gap.

00:16:26.720 --> 00:16:34.160
I think right now I'm sort of plastering over the cracks and when everybody leaves, then we'll just go and do it properly.

00:16:33.360 --> 00:16:36.960
But, today, it's just got to be done and look good quickly.

00:16:38.240 --> 00:16:47.680
With time running out, a trusty chair will have to do the job.

00:16:47.480 --> 00:16:51.320
But there's no time to sit around.

00:16:50.520 --> 00:16:58.400
The rooms aren't ready, and the supply car still hasn't arrived.

00:16:57.440 --> 00:17:02.960
They had a bit of a breakdown and so they're a bit late.

00:17:02.120 --> 00:17:07.960
But there's no loo paper, no tissues, you know, there's a lot of things we don't have right now.

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:11.240
We'll be scurrying around into all their rooms putting everything into place.

00:17:10.480 --> 00:17:12.119
Mummy, look.

00:17:11.240 --> 00:17:13.560
What happened?

00:17:14.800 --> 00:17:22.640
Only a few minutes from camp, Frank and the team are fitting Edison's tracking collar.

00:17:21.920 --> 00:17:28.200
So, this is a new type of collar that we're trialling.

00:17:27.440 --> 00:17:38.080
It's a little bit easier to put on than the other ones and instead of having a big lead weight at the bottom, all the brains are down in the weight as well.

00:17:37.560 --> 00:17:44.920
It may look big, but for an elephant it's just like wearing a watch.

00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:48.760
The collar's on.

00:17:47.880 --> 00:17:52.560
Now it's time to wake Edison up.

00:17:51.720 --> 00:17:57.880
So, we're just going to jump back in the car.

00:17:57.720 --> 00:17:59.040
That was...

00:17:58.200 --> 00:18:10.800
After 16 minutes, the antidote's just gone in so let's wait and see how long it takes him to wake up, and hopefully he does.

00:18:11.240 --> 00:18:12.360
The antidote counteracts the effects of the tranquilliser.

00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:17.960
All going to plan, Edison should be back on his feet within a couple of minutes.

00:18:17.440 --> 00:18:30.080
But he's not.

00:18:31.960 --> 00:18:46.360
This is when everything stops and everything gets quiet, and the second hand seems to go round the watch a bit slower... ..and you wait for him to get up.

00:18:47.520 --> 00:18:55.120
The first sign we'll be looking for is his ear twitching.

00:18:56.200 --> 00:19:00.720
It's normally just a couple of minutes, isn't it?

00:19:00.360 --> 00:19:02.480
He's been down too long and they're worried.

00:19:01.680 --> 00:19:21.320
Vet Matthew Mutinda administers another shot of antidote.

00:19:32.520 --> 00:19:37.240
Now my heart really is in my mouth.

00:19:36.400 --> 00:19:38.080
Have you seen this before, George?

00:19:37.880 --> 00:19:39.040
Er, yeah.

00:19:57.880 --> 00:20:00.560
I don't like this at all.

00:20:00.840 --> 00:20:05.960
He's took his time.

00:20:05.640 --> 00:20:09.120
Oh, thank God.

00:20:08.360 --> 00:20:14.640
Ah, that's a big relief.

00:20:16.200 --> 00:20:19.000
He's paying a lot of attention to it.

00:20:18.200 --> 00:20:24.920
He's sniffing it, thinking, "What the hell is this thing?

00:20:24.480 --> 00:20:29.960
Why am I wearing a necklace suddenly?"

00:20:33.240 --> 00:20:52.080
I've only done about ten of them, but every elephant that I have been involved in collaring leaves you with a special attachment to that elephant, so when you follow them on the tracking system, you know what they're like and you feel a connection, and certainly when you see them, you're very...

00:20:51.240 --> 00:20:54.880
It's like seeing an old friend again.

00:20:54.160 --> 00:21:00.400
So I'll always have a feeling for Edison now.

00:20:59.480 --> 00:21:09.640
Frank and the team have successfully collared an important bull elephant.

00:21:08.840 --> 00:21:19.000
Edison will now provide them with crucial data as he moves through the reserve and beyond.

00:21:25.880 --> 00:21:33.160
Back at camp, Saba's team has also succeeded.

00:21:32.400 --> 00:21:36.160
The tents are finished in the nick of time.

00:21:35.760 --> 00:21:43.240
I just feel like everything's kicking off, and it's quite exciting.

00:21:42.440 --> 00:21:49.320
We've worked so hard to get the camp ready today.

00:21:49.600 --> 00:22:01.160
The only thing still missing are the supplies, but for now the most important job is to make the guests feel welcome.

00:22:00.440 --> 00:22:04.400
Have you had a good day?

00:22:04.120 --> 00:22:05.960
Welcome.

00:22:05.040 --> 00:22:08.160
Hi, everyone!

00:22:07.280 --> 00:22:09.960
..But some of the team are here to welcome you.

00:22:09.200 --> 00:22:12.840
Sorry we're so late.

00:22:12.000 --> 00:22:14.480
Are you all ready for your showers and everything?

00:22:13.640 --> 00:22:15.040
Have you ordered them?

00:22:14.080 --> 00:22:17.240
We were going to eat now.

00:22:16.480 --> 00:22:17.800
Oh, you want to eat?

00:22:16.960 --> 00:22:19.080
And then go shower after.

00:22:18.120 --> 00:22:19.280
OK.

00:22:19.760 --> 00:22:27.160
The guests are settled, but Saba still has a long night ahead, not least because she's mum to three children.

00:22:26.320 --> 00:22:29.800
Just want to go and check on the kids quickly.

00:22:28.920 --> 00:22:37.040
I had to do everything in such a scramble, I didn't get a chance to say goodnight to them.

00:22:38.960 --> 00:22:40.240
Hi, sausage.

00:22:39.400 --> 00:22:43.000
I've come to say goodnight to my little girls.

00:22:42.120 --> 00:22:46.920
Can I have a hug, please, from my beautiful girls?

00:22:46.640 --> 00:22:50.160
Where's jungle baby?

00:22:50.680 --> 00:22:51.800
Where's your baby?

00:22:50.840 --> 00:22:52.840
I don't know, darling, where did you put your baby?

00:22:53.480 --> 00:22:56.040
Did you leave it behind?

00:22:55.080 --> 00:22:56.200
No.

00:22:55.320 --> 00:22:57.120
Hm?

00:22:58.920 --> 00:23:04.960
But just as it seems everything's under control...

00:23:04.400 --> 00:23:14.600
Did that light just go out?

00:23:13.920 --> 00:23:15.240
Oh...

00:23:14.440 --> 00:23:15.760
Is that the generator's gone off?

00:23:14.840 --> 00:23:23.240
Without the generator, there's no electricity in camp.

00:23:26.040 --> 00:23:31.200
Who switched it off?

00:23:30.440 --> 00:23:31.720
Me.

00:23:30.760 --> 00:23:33.200
Erm...

00:23:36.360 --> 00:23:44.440
I just thought everything was going so well today, and we'd finally cracked it all, and then this happens.

00:23:43.560 --> 00:23:47.320
And, of course, the supplies haven't arrived yet either.

00:23:46.600 --> 00:23:51.360
Do you know that nobody's got loo paper in their rooms?

00:23:50.520 --> 00:23:56.360
I've got, like, half a roll in number two and there's nothing in number one and nothing in number five.

00:23:56.520 --> 00:23:57.600
OK, so they're getting here.

00:23:58.200 --> 00:24:05.360
Luckily, they get it back up and running.

00:24:04.560 --> 00:24:06.440
I don't know what the hell is wrong with that machine.

00:24:05.760 --> 00:24:08.960
HARSH WHIRRING Oh, my God, that doesn't sound good.

00:24:08.160 --> 00:24:12.560
Despite the racket, camp has power again.

00:24:12.160 --> 00:24:21.960
I'm just going to get the guests at the dinner table and make sure that everything calms down, and I just hope that we're not going to lose power.

00:24:24.680 --> 00:24:34.040
Order is restored and, at last, the supplies arrive.

00:24:33.240 --> 00:24:49.600
For Simeon, one crucial thing is still missing.

00:24:54.080 --> 00:25:10.480
On the face of it, everything is going well.

00:25:16.160 --> 00:25:21.800
This is delicious.

00:25:24.400 --> 00:25:38.360
Yeah, it's lovely.

00:25:39.320 --> 00:25:46.880
It's been a hectic day and everyone could do with a good night's sleep.

00:25:47.200 --> 00:25:56.640
Saba and Frank have had a restless night.

00:25:58.480 --> 00:26:02.280
Oh, God, looks who's back.

00:26:01.600 --> 00:26:06.320
You noisy, noisy boy!

00:26:05.440 --> 00:26:10.040
I can't believe you kept us up all night.

00:26:10.320 --> 00:26:17.600
Sarara is a big male who regularly passes through camp.

00:26:16.720 --> 00:26:26.360
He's been tempted in by his favourite midnight snack - juicy acacia pods from the tree right outside their bedroom.

00:26:26.360 --> 00:26:30.360
This is the festivities of the night.

00:26:29.520 --> 00:26:32.120
Everything that's been going on.

00:26:32.360 --> 00:26:43.560
When they first started coming around, Frank and I were just like, "Whoo-hoo, this is so exciting," and now it's just been almost every night and we're exhausted!

00:26:42.800 --> 00:26:59.640
And last night I managed to find some earplugs, but even with earplugs stuffed into our ears, there were branches falling on the roof and he was shaking it, and rumbling and farting and, ugh, so noisy!

00:26:59.400 --> 00:27:15.160
He keeps us awake, but on the other side it's really nice that they trust us enough to be able to come here and feel safe, considering what's happening elsewhere in their range.

00:27:15.280 --> 00:27:26.120
I don't think the guests will mind, but luckily for them they don't have quite as close an experience because they've got these nice big verandas that keep the elephants at bay.

00:27:25.200 --> 00:27:39.320
His antics in camp may have kept the family up all night, but Saba's delighted when he sticks around to give her guests a very special elephant encounter... right over the breakfast table.

00:27:38.960 --> 00:27:41.520
This is really what this place is all about.

00:27:40.800 --> 00:27:54.080
You know, there's no boundaries, no fences between us and nature, and you get things like this happening, it's just magic!

00:27:54.360 --> 00:28:04.800
Saba hopes that if people see elephants up close like this, they'll want to help protect them.

00:28:05.080 --> 00:28:15.960
These unique experiences are key to the success of the business, and to securing a future with elephants.

00:28:15.000 --> 00:28:16.360
Next time...

00:28:19.320 --> 00:28:24.680
A member of the team is taken dangerously ill...

00:28:23.960 --> 00:28:29.240
I mean, the thing is, if you don't treat malaria, it can kill you.

00:28:29.560 --> 00:28:33.520
..Frank rushes to the rescue of an injured lioness...

00:28:32.760 --> 00:28:34.520
It's not looking very good.

00:28:33.680 --> 00:28:36.920
..And a power failure in camp leads to big trouble.

00:28:36.000 --> 00:28:39.160
It's going to be a big investment.

00:28:40.080 --> 00:28:41.760
Ugh.

00:29:43.040 --> 00:29:49.160
Treetop dining doesn't always go to plan...

00:29:55.440 --> 00:30:20.960
Magical movies this Christmas on BBC One.
